Portable libwebp decoder for the WikiReader
============================================

This directory contains the decoder-only subset of libwebp from
https://chromium.googlesource.com/webm/libwebp at main, commit
`1844042d1ca751e62e61df7617dba19c98588339` (2026-10-19), with the reader's
C33 changes applied: luma-only output, the IVRAM overlay sections, the
three-byte bit-reader refill, no gamma-compressed chroma (it needs pow()),
rescaler row loops that keep the scaling fields in registers, and irow/frow
interleaved (WEBP_RESCALER_ROW_STEP) so that reading both is one SDRAM
stream rather than two that evict each other's row, and an alpha palette
map that looks up a 256-byte copy of the palette's alpha in A0 RAM.

Only the generic C decoder, its utility code, and public headers are retained.
The encoder, mux/demux libraries, examples, tests, platform SIMD paths, and
threaded decoding are not part of the firmware build. `src/webp/config.h` is a
small freestanding configuration for this subset.

The upstream copyright and license are in COPYING. PATENTS contains the
upstream patent grant.
